  "details": "I have tested this out:\n\nhttps://github.com/philfiru/leapmotion-osc\n\nit allows you to use the leap motion on the front of the headset to have full finger tracking while still holding controllers.  I've tried this out while wearing index controllers and it is a huge step up.  It works wonderfully but it's a shame how much work you have to go through to get it to work what with needing to create a custom avatar to support it and needing to have external software running.  \n\nNow that the Leap Motion 2 has released, VRChat has already implemented quest hand tracking, and OSC support is so fleshed out, there is no better time than now where this should be supported.\n\nIf you implement native Leap Motion support, be sure to add functionality where controllers can be used for positional tracking, and leap motion is finger tracking.",
